WEBVTT

00:00:12.345 --> 00:00:13.642
Captain?

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:16.976
Report.

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:20.178
It looks like the Kazon
have retreated, Captain.

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:21.653
We must have hurt them.

00:00:21.688 --> 00:00:23.519
Not as bad as they hurt us.

00:00:23.556 --> 00:00:25.581
All engines are off-line.

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:28.651
Captain, shields are down,
as are all weapons arrays.

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:30.890
We'd better hope
they don't come back.

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:32.124
We're sitting ducks.

00:00:32.165 --> 00:00:33.359
Janeway to Engineering.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:34.458
What's your status?

00:00:34.501 --> 00:00:36.128
We're in bad shape, Captain.

00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:39.297
We had to shut down the warp
engines to avoid a breach.

00:00:39.339 --> 00:00:41.204
The impulse engines
are gone, too.

00:00:41.241 --> 00:00:43.004
I think
I can give you thrusters,

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:45.577
but I've got
a lot of casualties down here,

00:00:45.612 --> 00:00:47.136
I've got to tend to first.

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:48.875
Lieutenant, it's Kurt Bendera.

00:00:48.915 --> 00:00:50.280
He's hurt pretty bad.

00:00:50.316 --> 00:00:51.442
No.

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:52.542
His console exploded,

00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:53.847
caught him right in the face.

00:00:53.887 --> 00:00:56.355
We've got to get him
to Sick Bay right away.

00:00:56.389 --> 00:00:57.481
Torres to Sick Bay.

00:00:57.524 --> 00:00:59.424
I hope this is urgent,
Lieutenant.

00:00:59.459 --> 00:01:01.689
We have our hands full
at the moment.

00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:03.923
I'm sending up
an emergency transport.

00:01:03.963 --> 00:01:06.158
One of my people
is severely burned.

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:08.133
Very well.
We'll do what we can.

00:01:08.168 --> 00:01:10.159
More damage reports
coming in, Captain.

00:01:10.203 --> 00:01:11.966
There's a hull breach on Deck 4.

00:01:12.038 --> 00:01:13.198
Force field's in place.

00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:14.467
Repair crew's on the way.

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:16.304
There have been casualties
on all decks.

00:01:16.342 --> 00:01:17.331
No fatalities so far.

00:01:17.377 --> 00:01:18.901
Captain, request permission

00:01:18.945 --> 00:01:20.412
to give Torres a hand
in Engineering.

00:01:20.447 --> 00:01:22.381
Maybe I can help
get propulsion up and running.

00:01:22.415 --> 00:01:23.746
Good idea. Go ahead.

00:01:23.783 --> 00:01:25.546
Captain, my readings indicate

00:01:25.585 --> 00:01:28.383
the navigational deflector
has sustained massive damage.

00:01:28.421 --> 00:01:29.547
It will be necessary
to repair it

00:01:29.589 --> 00:01:31.784
before we can achieve
more than thruster power.

00:01:31.825 --> 00:01:33.087
Get repair crews on it.

00:01:33.126 --> 00:01:34.423
Mr. Kim, I want
a complete analysis

00:01:34.461 --> 00:01:36.224
of all the damage
we've sustained.

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:37.559
Yes, ma'am.

00:01:37.597 --> 00:01:38.825
He's not responding.

00:01:38.865 --> 00:01:40.492
75 milligrams of impedrezene.

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:42.467
That might help stimulate
his cardiac functions,

00:01:42.502 --> 00:01:43.969
but he sustained
so much injury,

00:01:44.003 --> 00:01:44.731
it may be too late.

00:01:44.771 --> 00:01:45.760
It had no effect.

00:01:45.805 --> 00:01:46.897
Cortical stimulator.

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:53.668
I'm sorry.

00:01:53.713 --> 00:01:55.544
He was too badly injured.

00:01:58.985 --> 00:02:00.953
He saved my life once...

00:02:00.987 --> 00:02:03.217
near the Cardassian border.

00:02:08.328 --> 00:02:09.556
Come in.

00:02:12.265 --> 00:02:14.460
Crewman Bendera's dead.

00:02:16.002 --> 00:02:17.902
The Doctor
couldn't do anything.

00:02:17.937 --> 00:02:19.962
I'm sorry, Chakotay.

00:02:20.039 --> 00:02:21.870
I know you were friends.

00:02:21.908 --> 00:02:25.275
Will you arrange
a memorial service?

00:02:25.311 --> 00:02:27.438
I'll get right on it.

00:02:30.016 --> 00:02:31.608
Was there something else?

00:02:31.651 --> 00:02:32.743
Yes.

00:02:32.785 --> 00:02:33.809
Like it or not,

00:02:33.853 --> 00:02:36.617
it seems we're in a situation
where the rules have changed,

00:02:36.656 --> 00:02:40.649
and, maybe, if we're going
to survive out here,

00:02:40.693 --> 00:02:42.991
we have to start changing, too.

00:02:43.096 --> 00:02:44.859
What do you mean?

00:02:45.932 --> 00:02:47.991
When we first started
our trip home,

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:49.625
you made a conscious decision

00:02:49.669 --> 00:02:51.466
to treat Voyager
as a Starfleet ship

00:02:51.504 --> 00:02:54.268
with a Starfleet crew
following Starfleet rules.

00:02:54.307 --> 00:02:55.638
That's right.

00:02:55.675 --> 00:02:59.406
Starfleet works well
in the Alpha Quadrant.

00:02:59.445 --> 00:03:01.606
But out here...

00:03:03.316 --> 00:03:05.750
maybe we should be thinking
more like the Maquis.

00:03:05.785 --> 00:03:09.243
The Maquis had to survive
on their own.

00:03:09.289 --> 00:03:11.450
We were up against
insurmountable odds.

00:03:11.491 --> 00:03:13.721
We had to create our own
opportunities for success

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:16.320
because nobody was willing
to help us.

00:03:16.362 --> 00:03:18.728
Sound like anybody you know?

00:03:18.765 --> 00:03:21.359
If you're suggesting
we abandon our principles

00:03:21.401 --> 00:03:23.096
just because
we're out of hailing range...

00:03:23.136 --> 00:03:26.799
Captain, this was the fourth
attack in two weeks.

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:29.137
We've lost three crew members
to the Kazon.

00:03:29.175 --> 00:03:31.666
A dozen more have sustained
serious injuries.

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:33.201
This ship has taken
so much damage,

00:03:33.246 --> 00:03:35.339
we'll be lucky to get warp drive
on line again,

00:03:35.381 --> 00:03:39.408
and we can count on the fact
that the Kazon will be back.

00:03:45.024 --> 00:03:48.460
I don't think we can afford
to keep doing business as usual.

00:05:46.178 --> 00:05:47.907
A lot of us can say
we're alive today

00:05:47.947 --> 00:05:49.847
because of Kurt Bendera.

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:53.975
There was never a better man
to have at your side,

00:05:54.019 --> 00:05:57.580
never anyone more willing
to take on the tough jobs.

00:05:57.623 --> 00:06:00.990
The first time I met him
was in a mining community

00:06:01.026 --> 00:06:02.891
on Telfas Prime.

00:06:02.928 --> 00:06:05.419
Some of the miners objected
to my sense of humor

00:06:05.464 --> 00:06:08.399
and decided they should break
a few of my bones.

00:06:08.434 --> 00:06:10.561
There were four of them
and one of me,

00:06:10.603 --> 00:06:12.161
and I was taking a beating.

00:06:12.204 --> 00:06:15.696
Suddenly, this man I'd never
seen before came out of nowhere

00:06:15.741 --> 00:06:17.868
and evened things up.

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:19.377
We stood back to back,

00:06:19.411 --> 00:06:21.936
and pretty soon
the others decided

00:06:21.981 --> 00:06:25.109
my sense of humor
wasn't so bad after all.

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:26.674
I thanked the man.

00:06:26.719 --> 00:06:28.914
He just grinned and said,

00:06:28.954 --> 00:06:31.218
"I like a good fight."

00:06:31.257 --> 00:06:34.886
He was my friend
from that moment on.

00:06:34.927 --> 00:06:37.657
And he kept fighting
the good fight...

00:06:37.696 --> 00:06:39.721
right up to the end.

00:06:44.069 --> 00:06:45.696
I'll miss him.

00:06:48.974 --> 00:06:50.464
Ensign.

00:07:05.591 --> 00:07:08.617
Captain,
can I ask you something?

00:07:08.661 --> 00:07:09.650
Of course.

00:07:09.695 --> 00:07:11.925
Now that the Kazon
have stepped up their attacks,

00:07:11.964 --> 00:07:13.454
a lot of people think
that we're not going

00:07:13.499 --> 00:07:14.591
to make it out of here alive.

00:07:14.633 --> 00:07:17.329
I'd like to know
what you have to say about that.

00:07:18.337 --> 00:07:20.897
Is there anything you
have to say about that?

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:23.568
I assure you,
you can speak freely.

00:07:23.609 --> 00:07:26.169
I'd give them what they want.

00:07:26.211 --> 00:07:27.940
Give them the replicators
and the transporters

00:07:27.980 --> 00:07:29.181
and whatever else

00:07:29.314 --> 00:07:30.576
it is they're after.

00:07:30.615 --> 00:07:33.083
I'm sure you realize
that would be a violation of...

00:07:33.118 --> 00:07:35.177
I know all about
the Prime Directive.

00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:36.551
But you know what?

00:07:36.588 --> 00:07:38.488
The Federation
is 70,000 light-years away.

00:07:38.523 --> 00:07:40.320
What does it matter
what these people do

00:07:40.358 --> 00:07:41.882
to each other
with our technology?

00:07:41.927 --> 00:07:44.054
I appreciate your concerns,
Crewman,

00:07:44.095 --> 00:07:46.757
but let me make it
absolutely clear...

00:07:46.798 --> 00:07:48.527
I'll destroy this ship

00:07:48.567 --> 00:07:51.331
before I turn any part of it
over to the Kazon.

00:07:56.875 --> 00:07:59.173
So that's how the Maquis
would do it, hmm?

00:08:06.785 --> 00:08:07.877
It's all right, Commander.

00:08:07.919 --> 00:08:08.886
I know Hogan's upset.

00:08:08.920 --> 00:08:10.581
He and Bendera were close.

00:08:10.622 --> 00:08:11.589
But that's not why he thinks

00:08:11.623 --> 00:08:13.022
we should give the Kazon
what they want.

00:08:13.058 --> 00:08:15.253
I think I've made
my position clear on that.

00:08:15.293 --> 00:08:17.420
You have, but a lot
of the crew feel

00:08:17.462 --> 00:08:19.327
they haven't had the chance
to voice their opinions.

00:08:19.364 --> 00:08:21.093
This isn't a democracy,
Chakotay.

00:08:21.132 --> 00:08:23.123
I can't run this ship
by consensus.

00:08:23.168 --> 00:08:24.294
A lot of the Maquis feel

00:08:24.336 --> 00:08:26.065
the Federation
abandoned them years ago.

00:08:26.104 --> 00:08:28.834
You may be willing to die
for Federation principles,

00:08:28.873 --> 00:08:30.932
but they're not.

00:08:31.009 --> 00:08:33.375
I can't believe you'd
support that man's position.

00:08:33.411 --> 00:08:35.572
I don't, but isn't
there something

00:08:35.614 --> 00:08:37.377
in between
your position and his?

00:08:40.652 --> 00:08:42.051
Deck 3.

00:08:42.087 --> 00:08:43.145
All I'm saying, Captain,

00:08:43.188 --> 00:08:45.520
is that maybe there's
a little room for flexibility

00:08:45.557 --> 00:08:47.718
in interpreting
Starfleet's protocols.

00:08:47.759 --> 00:08:49.590
Frankly, I'm not sure
they were ever intended

00:08:49.628 --> 00:08:50.652
for situations like this.

00:08:50.695 --> 00:08:52.959
I haven't seen any evidence
that they've let us down.

00:08:52.998 --> 00:08:54.659
Maybe this situation
with the Kazon

00:08:54.699 --> 00:08:55.757
is the first example.

00:08:55.800 --> 00:08:58.064
Maybe we have to examine
Starfleet's principles

00:08:58.103 --> 00:08:59.900
with a cold eye,
and ask ourselves

00:08:59.938 --> 00:09:01.599
if they're really
applicable here.

00:09:01.640 --> 00:09:04.074
Computer, hold turbolift.

00:09:04.109 --> 00:09:08.273
Commander, if you have
a specific suggestion

00:09:08.313 --> 00:09:09.780
please feel free to make it.

00:09:11.916 --> 00:09:14.214
Make a deal... an alliance.

00:09:15.387 --> 00:09:16.649
With the Kazon?

00:09:16.688 --> 00:09:18.588
With one of their factions,
or two.

00:09:18.623 --> 00:09:21.057
If we had the Ogla
and the Relora

00:09:21.092 --> 00:09:23.754
as our allies, the others
would be afraid to touch us.

00:09:23.795 --> 00:09:25.456
Nothing we've been through
with the Kazon

00:09:25.497 --> 00:09:27.055
would lead me to believe
they're trustworthy.

00:09:27.098 --> 00:09:29.032
I can't imagine making
a deal with them.

00:09:29.067 --> 00:09:30.625
With all due respect...

00:09:30.669 --> 00:09:32.637
maybe that's because
your imagination is limited

00:09:32.671 --> 00:09:33.660
by Starfleet protocols.

00:09:34.973 --> 00:09:38.101
As Captain, you're responsible
for making decisions

00:09:38.143 --> 00:09:40.043
in the best interest
of your crew,

00:09:40.078 --> 00:09:42.638
and I think you have
to ask yourself...

00:09:42.681 --> 00:09:45.081
if you're doing that.

00:09:59.264 --> 00:10:00.356
Come in.

00:10:03.668 --> 00:10:05.499
Captain.

00:10:05.537 --> 00:10:07.266
This is unexpected.

00:10:07.305 --> 00:10:09.170
I've been in your quarters
before.

00:10:09.207 --> 00:10:11.437
Indeed, but so rarely

00:10:11.476 --> 00:10:13.501
that I can remember
each instance.

00:10:13.545 --> 00:10:15.376
Vulcan spice tea... hot.

00:10:18.416 --> 00:10:20.077
And it was always
at a time when you were

00:10:20.118 --> 00:10:21.676
particularly troubled.

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:23.187
Right, as usual.

00:10:23.221 --> 00:10:25.485
Oh... thank you.

00:10:25.523 --> 00:10:27.718
Commander Chakotay has proposed

00:10:27.759 --> 00:10:30.956
that we make an alliance
with one of the Kazon factions.

00:10:30.995 --> 00:10:32.895
We wouldn't give them
weapons or technology,

00:10:32.931 --> 00:10:36.162
but we would pledge
to support and defend them

00:10:36.201 --> 00:10:37.634
if they're attacked.

00:10:37.669 --> 00:10:40.001
I am sure that made
you uncomfortable.

00:10:40.071 --> 00:10:41.766
How can I consider it?

00:10:41.806 --> 00:10:44.001
I can't just walk away
from the precepts

00:10:44.042 --> 00:10:45.976
Starfleet has laid out
for us...

00:10:46.010 --> 00:10:48.808
you don't deal with outlaws;
you don't involve yourself

00:10:48.847 --> 00:10:51.372
in the political machinations
of other cultures.

00:10:51.416 --> 00:10:52.849
It goes against
everything I believe,

00:10:52.884 --> 00:10:54.010
everything I've trained for,

00:10:54.052 --> 00:10:56.680
everything experience
has taught me.

00:10:56.721 --> 00:10:58.154
Quite right.

00:10:58.189 --> 00:11:00.282
Do I hear a "however" coming?

00:11:00.325 --> 00:11:03.385
You are perceptive, Captain.

00:11:03.428 --> 00:11:06.454
I believe Commander Chakotay's
suggestion does have merit.

00:11:07.665 --> 00:11:09.929
Help me understand that.

00:11:09.968 --> 00:11:13.404
When I was a young man,
a great visionary named Spock

00:11:13.438 --> 00:11:15.338
recommended an alliance
between the Federation

00:11:15.373 --> 00:11:17.637
and the Klingon Empire.

00:11:17.675 --> 00:11:19.472
This produced a major dispute.

00:11:19.511 --> 00:11:21.638
The Klingons, after all,
were outlaws,

00:11:21.679 --> 00:11:26.207
employing violence and brutality
in order to build their empire.

00:11:26.251 --> 00:11:28.947
I myself spoke out
against such a coalition,

00:11:28.987 --> 00:11:31.387
but the alliance was forged,

00:11:31.423 --> 00:11:33.220
and it brought a stability
to the Quadrant

00:11:33.258 --> 00:11:35.988
that had not been there
for 200 years.

00:11:36.027 --> 00:11:39.155
Spock's suggestion,
so controversial at first,

00:11:39.197 --> 00:11:41.757
proved to be the cornerstone
of peace.

00:11:41.800 --> 00:11:43.665
There are some differences here.

00:11:43.701 --> 00:11:46.169
By allying ourselves
to one faction,

00:11:46.204 --> 00:11:48.900
we'd be giving that faction
more power than the others.

00:11:48.940 --> 00:11:50.373
That would clearly affect

00:11:50.408 --> 00:11:53.002
the internal politics
of all the Kazon.

00:11:53.044 --> 00:11:55.012
I understand your concern,

00:11:55.079 --> 00:11:58.207
but, remember, it would only be
a temporary arrangement

00:11:58.249 --> 00:12:00.843
since we are on our way
out of this Quadrant.

00:12:00.885 --> 00:12:02.443
In the meantime,

00:12:02.487 --> 00:12:04.512
it might bring stability
to the region

00:12:04.556 --> 00:12:06.387
and security for us.

00:12:07.392 --> 00:12:08.359
Once we're gone,

00:12:08.393 --> 00:12:10.361
they'll probably go back
to their infighting.

00:12:10.395 --> 00:12:13.387
Perhaps.

00:12:13.431 --> 00:12:15.058
But even temporary stability

00:12:15.099 --> 00:12:17.465
can bring an appreciation
for peace.

00:12:19.704 --> 00:12:23.265
This flower is a rare hybrid.

00:12:23.308 --> 00:12:27.267
As far as I know, it exists
nowhere else in the galaxy.

00:12:27.312 --> 00:12:29.712
I created it
by grafting a cutting

00:12:29.747 --> 00:12:33.979
from a South American orchid
onto a Vulcan favinit plant.

00:12:34.018 --> 00:12:36.350
I doubted the graft would take,

00:12:36.387 --> 00:12:39.254
and, indeed, the plant
was sickly at first.

00:12:39.290 --> 00:12:41.986
However, after a few weeks,

00:12:42.026 --> 00:12:44.995
both plants adapted
to their new condition

00:12:45.063 --> 00:12:50.467
and, in fact, became stronger
than either had been alone.

00:12:52.971 --> 00:12:56.737
Consequently,
after much consideration,

00:12:56.774 --> 00:13:01.404
I've decided to seek an alliance
with one of the Kazon factions.

00:13:01.446 --> 00:13:03.346
Captain, you can't be serious.

00:13:03.381 --> 00:13:04.348
This goes against...

00:13:04.382 --> 00:13:05.349
Ensign...

00:13:05.383 --> 00:13:07.681
I'll be glad to discuss
my reasoning with you

00:13:07.719 --> 00:13:09.118
at a more appropriate time.

00:13:09.153 --> 00:13:11.485
However, this meeting is
not to debate the decision,

00:13:11.523 --> 00:13:13.787
but to decide how to pursue it.

00:13:13.825 --> 00:13:16.055
Captain... if I may.

00:13:16.094 --> 00:13:17.618
Yes, Mr. Neelix.

00:13:17.662 --> 00:13:21.428
We're not far from a
planet known as Sobras,

00:13:21.466 --> 00:13:23.263
where there's a Kazon settlement

00:13:23.301 --> 00:13:26.202
inhabited by a faction
known as the Pommar.

00:13:26.237 --> 00:13:27.966
I have an acquaintance there...

00:13:28.006 --> 00:13:29.906
someone who owes me some favors.

00:13:29.941 --> 00:13:32.432
Some rather large favors,
actually.

00:13:32.477 --> 00:13:35.241
Perhaps I could meet with him
and sound him out.

00:13:35.280 --> 00:13:37.305
Is he authorized
to speak for his maje?

00:13:37.348 --> 00:13:40.875
Not exactly, but he does
have the maje's ear.

00:13:40.919 --> 00:13:42.978
This would be
strictly informal,

00:13:43.021 --> 00:13:46.184
but it might give us a reading
on the possibility

00:13:46.224 --> 00:13:48.556
without the risk
of actual confrontation.

00:13:48.593 --> 00:13:49.753
Good idea.

00:13:49.794 --> 00:13:51.352
Proceed, Mr. Neelix.

00:13:51.396 --> 00:13:55.196
Why don't we just contact Seska
and form an alliance with her?

00:13:55.233 --> 00:13:57.360
Actually, that's a good idea.

00:13:57.402 --> 00:13:58.994
You've got to be kidding.

00:13:59.070 --> 00:14:00.970
Not at all.
Seska has been trying

00:14:01.005 --> 00:14:03.166
to forge an alliance
among the Kazon.

00:14:03.207 --> 00:14:05.208
She would jump at the chance
to get our support.

00:14:05.341 --> 00:14:06.171
She's right.

00:14:06.209 --> 00:14:07.301
If we went through Seska,

00:14:07.343 --> 00:14:09.573
at least we could ally ourselves
with the Nistrim.

00:14:09.612 --> 00:14:11.102
I think it's a bad idea.

00:14:11.147 --> 00:14:13.672
You can't have it both ways,
Commander.

00:14:13.716 --> 00:14:15.513
If you want to get in the mud
with the Kazon,

00:14:15.551 --> 00:14:17.917
you can't start complaining
that you might get dirty.

00:14:19.255 --> 00:14:21.485
Fine.
I'll talk with Seska.

00:14:21.524 --> 00:14:22.513
No.

00:14:22.558 --> 00:14:24.389
You've been through
too much with her.

00:14:24.427 --> 00:14:27.863
Mr. Neelix, prepare to take
your shuttle to Sobras.

00:14:27.897 --> 00:14:31.560
In the meantime, I'll
make contact with Seska.

00:14:31.601 --> 00:14:33.967
Dismissed.

00:14:45.915 --> 00:14:49.578
Captain's Log, Stardate 49337.4.

00:14:49.619 --> 00:14:51.348
After sending a subspace message

00:14:51.387 --> 00:14:53.787
to Seska
and the Nistrim Maje Culluh,

00:14:53.823 --> 00:14:55.984
we have a received
a quick response.

00:14:56.092 --> 00:14:57.616
Captain Janeway.

00:14:57.660 --> 00:15:00.458
Commander Chakotay.

00:15:00.496 --> 00:15:03.522
I must say we were surprised
to hear from you.

00:15:03.566 --> 00:15:05.397
Are you willing
to meet with us?

00:15:05.434 --> 00:15:07.299
You've made
an interesting proposal.

00:15:07.336 --> 00:15:09.327
I've discussed it with Seska,

00:15:09.372 --> 00:15:10.896
and she assures me
that you would not make

00:15:10.940 --> 00:15:13.841
this gesture
unless you were sincere.

00:15:13.876 --> 00:15:16.276
I will talk with you.

00:15:16.312 --> 00:15:17.836
I suggest we rendezvous.

00:15:17.880 --> 00:15:19.677
We'll transmit
coordinates to you.

00:15:19.715 --> 00:15:21.410
If you don't mind, Captain,

00:15:21.450 --> 00:15:22.940
we'd prefer to choose
the coordinates.

00:15:22.985 --> 00:15:25.647
Fine.
Transmit them to us.

00:15:25.688 --> 00:15:28.452
We'll meet
in approximately 20 hours.

00:15:28.491 --> 00:15:30.391
I must say, Captain,

00:15:30.426 --> 00:15:33.486
I look forward
to this opportunity.

00:16:04.627 --> 00:16:06.390
Hello, my friends.

00:16:06.429 --> 00:16:08.863
Please, don't let me interrupt.

00:16:13.402 --> 00:16:16.565
I was hoping to find
my good friend Jal Tersa here.

00:16:16.605 --> 00:16:18.368
Has he been in tonight?

00:16:20.443 --> 00:16:22.104
Thank you.

00:16:34.390 --> 00:16:35.584
Tersa, my friend.

00:16:37.226 --> 00:16:39.558
It could be dangerous
sneaking up on a man like that.

00:16:39.595 --> 00:16:41.688
I'd never dream
of sneaking up on you,

00:16:41.731 --> 00:16:43.426
but you were so engrossed in...

00:16:43.466 --> 00:16:44.956
whatever it is you're doing.

00:16:45.067 --> 00:16:47.194
A puzzle.

00:16:47.236 --> 00:16:49.602
What brings you here,
Talaxian?

00:16:49.638 --> 00:16:50.900
I'm good at puzzles.

00:16:50.940 --> 00:16:52.305
Perhaps I could help.

00:16:52.341 --> 00:16:54.741
The dancer showed it to me.

00:16:54.777 --> 00:16:56.244
By moving only two rods,

00:16:56.278 --> 00:16:58.439
this dodecahedron
can become an icosahedron.

00:16:58.481 --> 00:16:59.470
Hmm.

00:16:59.515 --> 00:17:02.245
She said she'd spend the night
with the man who could solve it.

00:17:03.319 --> 00:17:07.016
A splendid motivation,
to be sure.

00:17:07.056 --> 00:17:11.152
I just might be able

00:17:11.193 --> 00:17:13.058
to make your night
a memorable one.

00:17:13.095 --> 00:17:15.063
You know how to solve this?

00:17:15.097 --> 00:17:17.065
I might...

00:17:17.099 --> 00:17:18.464
if you'll hear me out first.

00:17:22.304 --> 00:17:26.468
My fortunes have changed
since we last met, Tersa.

00:17:26.509 --> 00:17:28.272
I've become a person
of some influence

00:17:28.310 --> 00:17:30.574
aboard a starship
known as Voyager.

00:17:31.614 --> 00:17:34.412
You must think us very isolated.

00:17:34.450 --> 00:17:35.417
Everyone knows that.

00:17:35.451 --> 00:17:38.147
It's probably the only reason
you were allowed in here,

00:17:38.187 --> 00:17:40.212
especially after last time.

00:17:41.290 --> 00:17:43.155
Oh.

00:17:43.192 --> 00:17:45.956
A simple misunderstanding.

00:17:46.061 --> 00:17:50.157
Uh... Tersa, I know you have
the ear of your first maje,

00:17:50.199 --> 00:17:52.099
as I do of our Captain.

00:17:52.134 --> 00:17:54.762
And we could be quite useful
to both of them.

00:17:54.804 --> 00:17:56.362
Go on.

00:17:56.405 --> 00:17:59.602
My Captain is interested
in talking to your maje

00:17:59.642 --> 00:18:02.372
to discuss a possible alliance.

00:18:02.411 --> 00:18:05.812
Do you think he'd have
any interest in such a meeting?

00:18:05.848 --> 00:18:07.440
An alliance?

00:18:07.483 --> 00:18:09.508
Between the Kazon-Pommar
and the Federations?

00:18:09.552 --> 00:18:11.918
An interesting thought,
isn't it?

00:18:12.021 --> 00:18:13.511
You're coming with us.

00:18:13.556 --> 00:18:16.150
Tersa, explain to them.

00:18:16.192 --> 00:18:17.250
We're friends.

00:18:17.293 --> 00:18:18.920
I have no idea
who this person is.

00:18:19.028 --> 00:18:22.054
Some lunatic who sat down
and started babbling.

00:18:22.097 --> 00:18:24.827
I guess you'll be spending
the night alone.

00:18:33.309 --> 00:18:36.437
You've made a good choice.

00:18:36.479 --> 00:18:39.880
The Nistrim will be
a potent ally.

00:18:39.915 --> 00:18:43.578
We want to make sure the Nistrim
will also be an honorable ally,

00:18:43.619 --> 00:18:47.282
that you'll adhere
to the conditions we establish.

00:18:47.323 --> 00:18:50.087
You can let
all the Kazon factions know

00:18:50.125 --> 00:18:52.093
that Voyager has formed
a coalition with you

00:18:52.127 --> 00:18:53.287
and will be an ally

00:18:53.329 --> 00:18:55.957
to any Nistrim ship
or outpost we encounter.

00:18:56.065 --> 00:18:58.966
In addition, we're prepared
to provide emergency supplies

00:18:59.001 --> 00:19:01.367
when needed...
food, medicine, clothing.

00:19:01.403 --> 00:19:02.495
What we will not provide

00:19:02.538 --> 00:19:05.006
is any of our technology
or weaponry.

00:19:05.040 --> 00:19:06.632
Understood.

00:19:06.675 --> 00:19:10.805
Just one other detail...

00:19:10.846 --> 00:19:13.178
an exchange of crew members.

00:19:13.215 --> 00:19:16.013
An exchange?

00:19:16.051 --> 00:19:17.245
Yes.

00:19:17.286 --> 00:19:19.777
I'm sure you'll agree
that our alliance

00:19:19.822 --> 00:19:22.313
should represent
a genuine partnership.

00:19:22.358 --> 00:19:24.656
Perhaps you should define that.

00:19:24.693 --> 00:19:26.217
It's obvious.

00:19:26.262 --> 00:19:28.787
Federation crew on my ship.

00:19:28.831 --> 00:19:31.391
Nistrim crew on yours.

00:19:31.433 --> 00:19:35.096
Maje, I think that's a detail
we could work out later.

00:19:35.137 --> 00:19:36.104
I can assure you

00:19:36.138 --> 00:19:38.436
that I would never agree
to that.

00:19:38.474 --> 00:19:41.875
It seems a natural extension
of your own proposal.

00:19:41.911 --> 00:19:44.106
We don't have to decide
everything right now.

00:19:44.146 --> 00:19:47.172
I will determine
what we decide and when.

00:19:48.784 --> 00:19:50.649
Yes, Maje.

00:19:50.686 --> 00:19:55.316
I won't have a woman
dictate terms to me.

00:19:55.357 --> 00:19:57.416
Culluh...

00:19:57.459 --> 00:19:58.687
I found the idea

00:19:58.727 --> 00:20:01.525
of an alliance
with you distasteful.

00:20:01.564 --> 00:20:04.192
I was willing to explore
the possibility,

00:20:04.233 --> 00:20:07.669
but now I see my instincts
were dead on.

00:20:07.703 --> 00:20:09.864
Talk to her.

00:20:09.905 --> 00:20:11.600
Tell her to be reasonable.

00:20:11.640 --> 00:20:13.301
This meeting is over.

00:20:22.885 --> 00:20:25.285
As soon as your maje learns
I'm being imprisoned,

00:20:25.321 --> 00:20:26.788
- he'll be outraged!
- Hurry up!

00:20:26.822 --> 00:20:27.789
He won't look kindly

00:20:27.823 --> 00:20:29.586
on anyone who's made
such an egregious error.

00:20:29.625 --> 00:20:31.786
What are you charging me with?!

00:20:33.796 --> 00:20:34.956
How long will I be held?

00:20:34.997 --> 00:20:36.123
Move.

00:20:36.165 --> 00:20:39.566
Well, I assume you'll at least
let me confer with counsel.

00:20:39.602 --> 00:20:43.129
I have the ability
to reward handsomely

00:20:43.172 --> 00:20:45.140
anyone who shows me
a bit of understanding.

00:20:47.676 --> 00:20:49.200
Is that a baby?

00:21:09.064 --> 00:21:10.895
My name is Neelix.

00:21:10.933 --> 00:21:13.060
I-I'm Talaxian.

00:21:13.102 --> 00:21:15.229
I'm Mabus.

00:21:15.270 --> 00:21:17.636
My friends and I are Trabe.

00:21:20.275 --> 00:21:21.742
They hurt you.

00:21:21.777 --> 00:21:25.144
I wasn't walking
quickly enough for them.

00:21:26.582 --> 00:21:27.981
Let's get the bleeding stopped.

00:21:28.017 --> 00:21:29.382
Then I'll clean it.

00:21:31.253 --> 00:21:32.880
Why are they holding you?

00:21:32.921 --> 00:21:35.685
They seem to be detaining
anyone who isn't Kazon.

00:21:35.724 --> 00:21:38.659
Several of our group
have been taken for questioning,

00:21:38.694 --> 00:21:40.719
but so far, none of them
have come back.

00:21:40.763 --> 00:21:42.663
How long have you been here?

00:21:42.698 --> 00:21:44.031
Five days.

00:21:44.164 --> 00:21:46.462
They attacked us in space.

00:21:46.500 --> 00:21:48.968
20 of our group died.

00:21:49.002 --> 00:21:51.664
We've lost nine more
since they put us in prison,

00:21:51.705 --> 00:21:53.570
including most of
the governing council.

00:21:53.607 --> 00:21:55.199
I'm the only one left.

00:21:55.242 --> 00:21:57.005
The Kazon won't be satisfied

00:21:57.077 --> 00:21:59.011
until you've all
been annihilated.

00:21:59.046 --> 00:22:01.708
If we've learned anything,
it's how to survive.

00:22:03.550 --> 00:22:05.916
Did you notice
how many guards they have posted

00:22:05.952 --> 00:22:07.078
at the entrance to the prison?

00:22:07.120 --> 00:22:09.315
Only two.
I guess they assume

00:22:09.356 --> 00:22:12.189
this place is so secure
they don't need any more.

00:22:12.225 --> 00:22:13.852
Why do you ask?

00:22:13.894 --> 00:22:17.091
We don't plan to sit here
while they kill us one by one.

00:22:17.130 --> 00:22:19.655
We were able
to get a message through

00:22:19.699 --> 00:22:22.224
to another Trabe vessel
before we were boarded.

00:22:22.269 --> 00:22:23.998
Help is on the way.

00:22:26.239 --> 00:22:27.831
Can we count on you?

00:22:31.511 --> 00:22:33.809
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:22:33.847 --> 00:22:36.338
We're on our way to rendezvous
with Mr. Neelix.

00:22:36.383 --> 00:22:38.248
I can only hope
that he had more luck

00:22:38.285 --> 00:22:39.912
with the Kazon than we did.

00:22:39.953 --> 00:22:42.421
Captain, we're approaching
the coordinates.

00:22:42.456 --> 00:22:43.889
All stop.

00:22:45.459 --> 00:22:46.983
I don't see any trace of him.

00:22:47.060 --> 00:22:49.927
Long-range sensors indicate
no sign of Mr. Neelix's shuttle

00:22:49.963 --> 00:22:51.828
within a radius
of two light-years.

00:22:51.865 --> 00:22:53.662
The Kazon have him.

00:22:53.700 --> 00:22:56.260
We cannot jump to conclusions.

00:22:56.303 --> 00:22:57.861
He may simply have been delayed.

00:23:00.307 --> 00:23:02.468
We'll hold position here
for two hours.

00:23:02.509 --> 00:23:06.036
If he hasn't shown up by then,
we'll go to Sobras.

00:23:19.159 --> 00:23:22.856
Lieutenant, could you
fill us in a little?

00:23:22.896 --> 00:23:24.955
There are all kinds of rumors
flying around

00:23:25.031 --> 00:23:26.760
about what's going on
with the Kazon.

00:23:26.800 --> 00:23:28.233
Nothing's going on yet.

00:23:28.268 --> 00:23:31.294
The Captain's talk with Seska
fell apart pretty quickly.

00:23:31.338 --> 00:23:33.772
Nothing's going
to come of all this.

00:23:33.807 --> 00:23:36.207
B'Elanna, you were
Seska's friend.

00:23:36.243 --> 00:23:38.507
Couldn't you get word to her,
try to work things out?

00:23:38.545 --> 00:23:39.637
No, I couldn't.

00:23:39.679 --> 00:23:40.646
I don't understand...

00:23:40.680 --> 00:23:42.238
Hogan, it's gone too far.

00:23:42.282 --> 00:23:44.580
Seska isn't the person
we thought she was.

00:23:44.618 --> 00:23:47.382
I don't trust her anymore.

00:23:47.420 --> 00:23:51.550
Even if it means
us getting home in one piece...

00:23:51.591 --> 00:23:53.991
or do you agree
with our Captain

00:23:54.060 --> 00:23:56.893
that holding onto our technology
is worth dying for?

00:23:56.930 --> 00:23:58.989
Who are you to be second-
guessing Captain Janeway?

00:23:59.032 --> 00:24:00.499
The hardest thing
you have to worry about

00:24:00.534 --> 00:24:02.331
is keeping
that dilithium chamber filled.

00:24:02.369 --> 00:24:03.927
She is doing the best she can
to get us home,

00:24:04.004 --> 00:24:05.596
and if you don't like
the way she's doing it,

00:24:05.639 --> 00:24:07.573
I really don't want
to hear about it.

00:24:07.607 --> 00:24:10.474
Is that clear?

00:24:10.510 --> 00:24:12.808
Perfectly.

00:24:20.987 --> 00:24:22.921
Some of the children
are too weak to run.

00:24:22.956 --> 00:24:24.048
We'll have to carry them.

00:24:24.090 --> 00:24:26.388
We can use another
pair of strong arms.

00:24:26.426 --> 00:24:28.121
You can count on me.

00:24:28.161 --> 00:24:30.356
I can't promise we'll
get out of here alive,

00:24:30.397 --> 00:24:32.695
but if we stay here,
we'll die anyway.

00:24:32.732 --> 00:24:34.996
I'd rather go out
fighting, myself.

00:24:37.971 --> 00:24:39.871
That one might be a problem.

00:24:39.906 --> 00:24:42.238
He's the kind
who'll start shooting

00:24:42.275 --> 00:24:44.209
at the first sign of trouble.

00:24:44.244 --> 00:24:45.336
I'll keep an eye on him.

00:24:51.284 --> 00:24:52.444
This may be it.

00:24:52.485 --> 00:24:53.679
Be ready.

00:24:56.523 --> 00:24:58.115
Stay back.

00:25:11.438 --> 00:25:12.837
Get back!

00:25:12.872 --> 00:25:14.669
Against the walls.

00:25:24.150 --> 00:25:25.117
Now!

00:25:25.151 --> 00:25:26.550
Let's go, let's go... come on!

00:25:26.586 --> 00:25:27.575
Come on, everyone, let's go.

00:25:27.621 --> 00:25:28.610
Come on!

00:25:29.990 --> 00:25:30.957
Let's go.

00:25:30.991 --> 00:25:32.185
Come on.

00:25:33.426 --> 00:25:35.257
Come on.

00:25:35.295 --> 00:25:36.262
Nice work, my friends.

00:25:36.296 --> 00:25:37.263
Let's go.

00:25:37.297 --> 00:25:38.286
Come on.

00:25:46.640 --> 00:25:48.767
All right, that's it.
We're going after him.

00:25:48.808 --> 00:25:50.901
Mr. Paris, set a course
for Sobras, full impulse.

00:25:50.944 --> 00:25:51.911
Aye, Captain.

00:25:51.945 --> 00:25:52.934
Tuvok, arm the phaser banks

00:25:52.979 --> 00:25:54.207
and load the forward
torpedo bays.

00:25:54.247 --> 00:25:56.340
We don't know what the Kazon
have in store for us.

00:25:56.383 --> 00:25:58.374
Shields at full power.

00:25:58.418 --> 00:26:00.613
Yellow Alert.
All hands at the ready.

00:26:00.654 --> 00:26:01.951
Captain.

00:26:01.988 --> 00:26:03.353
What is it?

00:26:03.390 --> 00:26:04.550
Ships.

00:26:04.591 --> 00:26:06.616
Kazon ships
on long-range sensors.

00:26:06.660 --> 00:26:07.752
Closing fast.

00:26:07.794 --> 00:26:09.159
Confirmed, Captain.

00:26:09.195 --> 00:26:10.890
On screen.

00:26:12.632 --> 00:26:16.363
It appears to be an armada,
and their weapons are powered.

00:26:16.403 --> 00:26:17.529
Red Alert.

00:26:28.014 --> 00:26:30.915
Power all weapon systems
and stand ready.

00:26:30.950 --> 00:26:33.214
Mr. Kim, hail the lead ship.

00:26:33.253 --> 00:26:34.743
They're hailing us, Captain.

00:26:34.788 --> 00:26:36.619
I'll put it on screen.

00:26:36.656 --> 00:26:38.749
Hello, Captain.

00:26:38.792 --> 00:26:41.352
I'd like you to meet
my good friend Mabus.

00:26:41.394 --> 00:26:44.227
We've just escaped
from the Kazon-Pommar.

00:26:44.264 --> 00:26:45.959
What are you doing
on a Kazon ship?

00:26:45.999 --> 00:26:48.263
They're Trabe vessels, actually.

00:26:48.301 --> 00:26:51.293
Everything the Kazon have,
they stole from the Trabe.

00:26:51.338 --> 00:26:54.398
Mabus will tell you all about it
over a sumptuous dinner.

00:26:54.441 --> 00:26:57.069
The food hasn't been
very good where we've been.

00:26:57.110 --> 00:27:00.409
I look forward to it.

00:27:04.417 --> 00:27:06.078
I was eight years old
when it started.

00:27:06.119 --> 00:27:08.417
I wasn't even
particularly aware of the Kazon.

00:27:10.457 --> 00:27:12.357
They lived in restricted areas

00:27:12.392 --> 00:27:14.986
that children
weren't allowed to go near.

00:27:18.565 --> 00:27:22.194
I didn't know they lived
in poverty, and filth...

00:27:24.304 --> 00:27:27.671
I didn't know they were
persecuted by the Trabe police.

00:27:28.975 --> 00:27:31.842
I was told they were violent
and dangerous

00:27:31.878 --> 00:27:34.369
and had to be kept isolated,

00:27:34.414 --> 00:27:36.848
so they wouldn't get loose
and kill us,

00:27:36.883 --> 00:27:39.215
which is exactly what they did,

00:27:39.252 --> 00:27:41.743
but we brought it on ourselves.

00:27:41.788 --> 00:27:43.813
The Trabe treated them
like animals...

00:27:43.857 --> 00:27:46.917
fenced them in, encouraged them
to fight amongst themselves

00:27:46.960 --> 00:27:48.393
so they wouldn't turn on us

00:27:48.428 --> 00:27:53.695
and sat by while they turned
into a violent, angry army.

00:27:53.733 --> 00:27:56.531
When they finally realized
we were their true enemy,

00:27:56.569 --> 00:27:58.560
we didn't stand a chance.

00:27:58.605 --> 00:27:59.697
I was luckier than most.

00:27:59.739 --> 00:28:01.263
A friend's father
grabbed me and took me

00:28:01.307 --> 00:28:03.332
with his family to
one of the starships

00:28:03.376 --> 00:28:04.604
that managed to escape.

00:28:04.644 --> 00:28:06.134
I can still remember...

00:28:06.179 --> 00:28:08.170
it happened so fast.

00:28:08.214 --> 00:28:09.841
One minute...

00:28:09.883 --> 00:28:14.013
I was a happy child
playing in a field;

00:28:14.053 --> 00:28:18.090
the next, an orphan,
exiled in space.

00:28:18.223 --> 00:28:21.681
It strikes me that in many ways,

00:28:21.726 --> 00:28:23.660
we're in the same predicament...

00:28:23.695 --> 00:28:26.755
separated from the lives
we knew,

00:28:26.798 --> 00:28:28.390
searching for home.

00:28:31.670 --> 00:28:34.070
A goal you may well achieve,
Captain,

00:28:34.106 --> 00:28:35.539
but the Kazon have refused

00:28:35.574 --> 00:28:37.565
to allow us to find
a new homeworld.

00:28:37.609 --> 00:28:39.406
Every time we try
to settle somewhere,

00:28:39.444 --> 00:28:41.708
they attack and drive us away.

00:28:41.746 --> 00:28:46.342
We're scattered, like nomads,
with no home and little hope.

00:28:49.688 --> 00:28:51.713
It happened over 30 years ago

00:28:51.756 --> 00:28:53.724
and the Kazon are still
trying to punish you?

00:28:53.758 --> 00:28:55.953
Remarkable, isn't it?

00:28:56.027 --> 00:28:59.519
Most of the Trabe
who persecuted the Kazon

00:28:59.564 --> 00:29:02.089
are either dead
or old men by now.

00:29:02.134 --> 00:29:05.831
Most of us were children
when the uprising occurred,

00:29:05.871 --> 00:29:08.738
and our children are innocent,

00:29:08.773 --> 00:29:11.742
but the Kazon's
desire for revenge

00:29:11.776 --> 00:29:13.676
is as strong as ever.

00:29:20.552 --> 00:29:23.214
How are you able to transmit to
us without your crew knowing it?

00:29:23.255 --> 00:29:24.620
Well, that's for me
to worry about.

00:29:24.656 --> 00:29:28.922
Let's just say I'm very familiar
with communications protocols.

00:29:29.027 --> 00:29:32.485
Now, will you let me talk
to Seska?

00:29:32.531 --> 00:29:35.659
Not without some proof
you can be trusted.

00:29:35.700 --> 00:29:37.497
She and I knew each other
for a long time.

00:29:37.536 --> 00:29:39.333
She knows that I can be trusted.

00:29:39.371 --> 00:29:40.429
Just let me talk to her.

00:29:40.472 --> 00:29:42.940
I'll convey your message.

00:29:42.974 --> 00:29:44.703
Contact me tomorrow,
and I'll let you know

00:29:44.743 --> 00:29:46.438
if she's willing to talk to you.

00:29:56.188 --> 00:29:57.746
Before the uprising,

00:29:57.789 --> 00:30:00.622
the Trabe were known
as a highly evolved species.

00:30:00.659 --> 00:30:02.490
They produced scholars
and artists

00:30:02.527 --> 00:30:03.858
who were widely admired,

00:30:03.895 --> 00:30:07.092
and their technology was among
the finest in the Quadrant.

00:30:07.132 --> 00:30:09.692
No one really knew
about the Kazon

00:30:09.734 --> 00:30:12.168
and how they were being treated.

00:30:12.204 --> 00:30:13.171
Why not?

00:30:13.205 --> 00:30:14.968
Holding another culture
in virtual slavery

00:30:15.006 --> 00:30:17.099
isn't the kind of thing
that would go unnoticed.

00:30:17.142 --> 00:30:18.666
You have to understand,

00:30:18.710 --> 00:30:20.644
the Trabe were rich
and powerful.

00:30:20.679 --> 00:30:21.976
They manipulated information

00:30:22.013 --> 00:30:23.708
about the conditions
on their planet,

00:30:23.748 --> 00:30:26.080
and no one wanted to risk
offending them

00:30:26.117 --> 00:30:28.142
and losing opportunities
for trade.

00:30:28.186 --> 00:30:30.484
It seems to me that they've
learned their lesson.

00:30:30.522 --> 00:30:32.353
Mabus and his people
have freely acknowledged

00:30:32.390 --> 00:30:34.585
that they were responsible
for what happened to them.

00:30:34.626 --> 00:30:36.821
Still, I do not see that

00:30:36.861 --> 00:30:39.261
it is a particularly good
idea to form an alliance

00:30:39.297 --> 00:30:40.628
with the blood-enemies
of the Kazon.

00:30:40.665 --> 00:30:43.429
We risk uniting
all the factions against us.

00:30:43.468 --> 00:30:45.663
The only thing
the Kazon agree on now

00:30:45.704 --> 00:30:47.763
is that we
are their common enemy.

00:30:47.806 --> 00:30:49.933
It's hard to imagine
it getting much worse.

00:30:49.975 --> 00:30:50.964
The Trabe have a lot of ships

00:30:51.009 --> 00:30:52.840
and a lot of weapons
in that convoy.

00:30:52.877 --> 00:30:55.437
I think this alliance would be
better than none at all.

00:30:55.480 --> 00:30:56.947
I'd rather not be
in the position

00:30:56.982 --> 00:30:58.347
of making an alliance at all,

00:30:58.383 --> 00:31:02.319
but that may be a luxury
we simply don't have.

00:31:02.354 --> 00:31:07.087
My gut tells me we don't have
any friends among the Kazon.

00:31:07.125 --> 00:31:09.593
As for the Trabe...

00:31:09.628 --> 00:31:12.119
I believe that people have
a capacity to change.

00:31:12.163 --> 00:31:13.755
It's always been
Starfleet's policy

00:31:13.798 --> 00:31:14.924
to deal with new species

00:31:14.966 --> 00:31:17.628
on a basis of openness
and trust...

00:31:17.669 --> 00:31:19.534
until proven otherwise.

00:31:25.377 --> 00:31:27.436
Captain, I'm glad to see you.

00:31:27.479 --> 00:31:28.446
I wanted to thank you

00:31:28.480 --> 00:31:30.345
for the use
of your medical facilities.

00:31:30.382 --> 00:31:32.509
We have very few doctors.

00:31:32.550 --> 00:31:34.745
Everyone seems to be
in generally good condition.

00:31:34.786 --> 00:31:36.845
Malnutrition
is the most common problem,

00:31:36.888 --> 00:31:39.618
but it's easily alleviated
with bio-nutrient supplements.

00:31:39.658 --> 00:31:40.625
Thank you, Doctor.

00:31:40.659 --> 00:31:41.626
How much longer do you need?

00:31:41.660 --> 00:31:43.628
I'd say less than an hour.

00:31:43.662 --> 00:31:45.289
Will you walk with me?

00:31:45.330 --> 00:31:46.319
Of course.

00:31:50.402 --> 00:31:52.199
I've been thinking...

00:31:52.237 --> 00:31:54.330
about our conversation
at dinner.

00:31:54.372 --> 00:31:55.339
Mm-hmm.

00:31:55.373 --> 00:31:58.171
About the things we share,
and it seems to me

00:31:58.209 --> 00:32:00.404
we could be of mutual
benefit to each other.

00:32:00.445 --> 00:32:01.935
Go on.

00:32:01.980 --> 00:32:02.947
What would you say

00:32:02.981 --> 00:32:05.313
to the possibility
of our joining forces...

00:32:05.350 --> 00:32:07.750
my starship and your convoy?

00:32:07.786 --> 00:32:10.448
Clearly we'd be a stronger
force if we did that.

00:32:10.488 --> 00:32:11.546
We could travel together

00:32:11.589 --> 00:32:13.716
for as long as it's
advantageous to both of us.

00:32:13.758 --> 00:32:16.591
Maybe we'll find our way
out of Kazon territory,

00:32:16.628 --> 00:32:19.392
and you could settle
on a new homeworld.

00:32:19.431 --> 00:32:21.058
It's a reasonable idea, Captain.

00:32:21.099 --> 00:32:22.157
I have no objection,

00:32:22.200 --> 00:32:24.293
but it would only benefit
your group and mine.

00:32:24.336 --> 00:32:25.303
There are other Trabe

00:32:25.337 --> 00:32:27.202
who wouldn't enjoy
the same protection.

00:32:27.238 --> 00:32:29.502
I wonder...

00:32:29.541 --> 00:32:32.874
if you might consider a
somewhat more... bold plan.

00:32:32.911 --> 00:32:34.572
Tell me.

00:32:34.612 --> 00:32:35.977
Together, Voyager and the Trabe

00:32:36.014 --> 00:32:37.709
would be a force
to be reckoned with.

00:32:37.749 --> 00:32:39.614
Suppose we took
advantage of that

00:32:39.651 --> 00:32:42.347
and asked the representatives
of all the Kazon factions

00:32:42.387 --> 00:32:44.412
to join us
at the bargaining table.

00:32:44.456 --> 00:32:47.516
In order to achieve what?

00:32:47.559 --> 00:32:48.890
Peace.

00:32:48.927 --> 00:32:51.259
Together, we would represent
a stabilizing force

00:32:51.296 --> 00:32:52.786
in this part of the Quadrant...

00:32:52.831 --> 00:32:54.594
bring the factions together,

00:32:54.632 --> 00:32:56.532
convince them
that an end to violence

00:32:56.568 --> 00:32:58.502
would be in everyone's
best interest.

00:32:58.536 --> 00:33:00.902
Think about it.

00:33:00.939 --> 00:33:02.930
I believe it could work.

00:33:02.974 --> 00:33:05.238
It's a message from Voyager.

00:33:06.378 --> 00:33:09.609
They've formed an alliance...
with the Trabe!

00:33:09.647 --> 00:33:11.444
The Trabe?

00:33:11.483 --> 00:33:16.284
They're calling for a conference
of all first majes.

00:33:16.321 --> 00:33:18.221
How could this have happened?

00:33:18.256 --> 00:33:21.521
It happened because you
let Voyager slip away,

00:33:21.559 --> 00:33:23.424
right into the hands
of the Trabe,

00:33:23.461 --> 00:33:26.726
by insisting on that
ridiculous exchange of crews.

00:33:26.765 --> 00:33:29.495
I could not let
the negotiations

00:33:29.534 --> 00:33:31.399
be dictated by that woman.

00:33:31.436 --> 00:33:34.337
That's becoming
a tired refrain, Culluh.

00:33:34.372 --> 00:33:36.897
One day that attitude
will be your undoing.

00:33:36.941 --> 00:33:38.841
Watch your tongue.

00:33:40.011 --> 00:33:41.706
Or what?

00:33:41.746 --> 00:33:44.579
I'm carrying your child.

00:33:44.616 --> 00:33:47.949
I don't think you'd do anything
to jeopardize him.

00:33:49.954 --> 00:33:51.979
We can still turn this
to our advantage.

00:33:52.023 --> 00:33:53.888
We have a crewman on Voyager

00:33:53.925 --> 00:33:56.826
who's willing to provide
information to us.

00:33:56.861 --> 00:33:59.796
There's long-term potential
in that arrangement.

00:33:59.831 --> 00:34:01.662
We mustn't lose sight of it.

00:34:01.699 --> 00:34:04.896
You're not suggesting
we go to this conference...

00:34:04.936 --> 00:34:07.063
that we come running
like a Calogan dog

00:34:07.105 --> 00:34:08.697
when the Federations call?

00:34:08.740 --> 00:34:12.039
Could you risk being the only
maje who doesn't attend?

00:34:12.076 --> 00:34:15.045
Of course you'll go

00:34:15.079 --> 00:34:16.603
and listen.

00:34:16.648 --> 00:34:19.082
Nothing should be
negotiated there...

00:34:19.117 --> 00:34:21.381
not at the point
of a Federation weapon,

00:34:21.419 --> 00:34:23.649
but you can learn a great deal,

00:34:23.688 --> 00:34:26.657
assess the mood
of the other majes.

00:34:26.691 --> 00:34:29.489
Find out the strength
of the Trabe convoy.

00:34:31.729 --> 00:34:33.526
You may be right.

00:34:33.565 --> 00:34:36.728
You can come out of this a hero.

00:34:36.768 --> 00:34:41.728
You can use this conference
to unite the factions,

00:34:41.773 --> 00:34:45.470
eradicate the Trabe
once and for all,

00:34:45.510 --> 00:34:49.310
and take Voyager as a trophy.

00:34:49.347 --> 00:34:51.178
Ooh.

00:34:54.285 --> 00:34:57.777
Captain's Log, Stardate 49342.5.

00:34:57.822 --> 00:35:00.518
Neelix has returned from Sobras
where he learned

00:35:00.558 --> 00:35:02.617
a disturbing piece
of information

00:35:02.660 --> 00:35:05.288
that may require us
to rethink our plans.

00:35:05.330 --> 00:35:06.922
He was a Takrit...

00:35:06.965 --> 00:35:09.934
a band of mercenaries
that operates in this system.

00:35:10.001 --> 00:35:10.933
What was he doing

00:35:11.002 --> 00:35:12.469
when the Kazon-Pommar
arrested him?

00:35:12.504 --> 00:35:16.005
My contact on the planet said
that he was making a sketch

00:35:16.138 --> 00:35:17.765
of the conference site,
and believe me,

00:35:17.806 --> 00:35:19.637
the Takrit are not
known for their art.

00:35:19.675 --> 00:35:21.040
Who sent him?

00:35:21.076 --> 00:35:22.941
That's as much information
as I got.

00:35:23.045 --> 00:35:25.946
So someone wants to sabotage
this conference.

00:35:25.981 --> 00:35:27.881
One of the majes.

00:35:27.916 --> 00:35:29.406
Why miss a chance
to wipe out your rivals

00:35:29.451 --> 00:35:31.316
while they're together
in one room?

00:35:31.353 --> 00:35:32.320
If that is true,

00:35:32.354 --> 00:35:34.254
then one of them will
undoubtedly try to leave

00:35:34.289 --> 00:35:35.586
before the meeting is finished.

00:35:35.624 --> 00:35:37.182
Captain, I think you
should consider

00:35:37.226 --> 00:35:38.488
not going to the conference.

00:35:39.495 --> 00:35:42.589
No. If I can help bring
stability to this Quadrant,

00:35:42.631 --> 00:35:45.464
I'm not going to walk away
because of a rumor.

00:35:45.501 --> 00:35:48.664
A rumor that must be taken
seriously, nonetheless.

00:35:48.704 --> 00:35:50.069
Agreed.

00:35:51.173 --> 00:35:52.868
Commander...

00:35:52.908 --> 00:35:56.241
monitor all the Kazon vessels
carefully

00:35:56.278 --> 00:35:58.109
and look out for any
suspicious ship movement

00:35:58.147 --> 00:35:59.136
near the surface.

00:35:59.181 --> 00:36:01.240
Keep us on a constant
transporter lock

00:36:01.283 --> 00:36:03.547
so we can beam out
at the first hint of trouble.

00:36:03.585 --> 00:36:07.351
Tuvok, Neelix, you're with me.

00:36:21.537 --> 00:36:24.097
I gave a great deal of thought
to the shape of the table.

00:36:24.139 --> 00:36:26.607
I finally decided on a triangle.

00:36:26.642 --> 00:36:28.234
Your group would
sit on one side.

00:36:28.277 --> 00:36:30.074
The majes would
occupy the other two.

00:36:30.112 --> 00:36:32.740
Does that seem appropriate?

00:36:32.781 --> 00:36:37.718
Have you heard anything more
about the matter we discussed?

00:36:37.753 --> 00:36:39.618
Don't talk about that here.

00:36:39.655 --> 00:36:40.952
It could mean my head.

00:36:40.989 --> 00:36:44.720
Does the table shape
seem acceptable?

00:36:44.760 --> 00:36:47.251
Tersa, this time I am here
with a powerful starship.

00:36:47.296 --> 00:36:49.560
You better be telling me
everything you know.

00:36:49.598 --> 00:36:51.156
I am, I swear.

00:36:51.200 --> 00:36:53.964
I want to thank you
for making it possible

00:36:54.069 --> 00:36:56.060
to have the conference
here on Sobras.

00:36:56.105 --> 00:36:57.970
My maje has
rewarded me handsomely

00:36:58.040 --> 00:36:59.837
for the prestige
it affords him.

00:36:59.875 --> 00:37:02.901
If there is any further way
I can be of service,

00:37:03.011 --> 00:37:04.774
please let me know.

00:37:10.686 --> 00:37:12.654
He hasn't heard anything more,
but he's frightened.

00:37:12.688 --> 00:37:15.657
He must believe
something's going to happen.

00:37:17.259 --> 00:37:20.490
The first majes
of the Kazon Order.

00:37:22.698 --> 00:37:25.428
Minnis of the Pommar.

00:37:29.638 --> 00:37:31.970
Surat of the Mostral.

00:37:36.445 --> 00:37:38.777
Loran of the Hobii.

00:37:43.051 --> 00:37:45.815
Valek of the Oglamar.

00:37:49.324 --> 00:37:51.792
And Culluh of the Nistrim.

00:37:55.864 --> 00:37:59.595
Captain, we seem destined
to encounter each other.

00:37:59.635 --> 00:38:03.230
This is Mabus,
a governor of the Trabe.

00:38:03.272 --> 00:38:06.639
Maje Culluh, I'm gratified
to be meeting you like this.

00:38:06.675 --> 00:38:08.905
I hope we'll be able
to come to terms.

00:38:08.944 --> 00:38:11.003
I never thought I'd see the day

00:38:11.046 --> 00:38:14.777
when any of us would sit
at a table with the Trabe.

00:38:14.816 --> 00:38:16.545
Times change, Maje.

00:38:16.585 --> 00:38:18.075
Perhaps.

00:38:18.120 --> 00:38:19.348
Shall we?

00:38:24.459 --> 00:38:27.895
Our gracious host, Jal Minnis,
has provided food and drink

00:38:27.930 --> 00:38:30.057
to make our discussions
more pleasant.

00:38:30.098 --> 00:38:32.362
We appreciate your coming.

00:38:32.401 --> 00:38:35.928
We hope this will lead
to a new climate of peace.

00:38:36.038 --> 00:38:37.562
Peace?

00:38:37.606 --> 00:38:39.039
With the Trabe?

00:38:39.074 --> 00:38:41.099
Forgive me if I'm
a bit skeptical.

00:38:41.143 --> 00:38:42.770
I understand.

00:38:42.811 --> 00:38:46.406
After decades of antagonism,
you're bound to be suspicious.

00:38:46.448 --> 00:38:51.647
But surely, everyone here is
tired of constant violence.

00:38:51.687 --> 00:38:55.589
Aren't you really trying
to get us to relax our guard

00:38:55.624 --> 00:38:58.525
so the Trabe
can conquer us again?

00:38:58.560 --> 00:38:59.652
How could we do that?

00:38:59.695 --> 00:39:01.185
We're scattered and dispirit.

00:39:01.230 --> 00:39:03.892
All we ask for
is a chance to find

00:39:03.966 --> 00:39:07.060
a new homeworld
and settle peacefully.

00:39:07.102 --> 00:39:08.660
Excuse me.

00:39:17.412 --> 00:39:20.404
Captain Janeway,
I'm curious as to the nature

00:39:20.449 --> 00:39:23.145
of this alliance
you've struck with the Trabe.

00:39:24.686 --> 00:39:28.053
Especially since you refused
my offer of a similar pact.

00:39:28.090 --> 00:39:32.424
I found the goals of the Trabe
to be compatible with our own.

00:39:32.461 --> 00:39:34.895
I represent an organization
which is devoted

00:39:34.930 --> 00:39:36.693
to peaceful coexistence
among people.

00:39:36.732 --> 00:39:38.597
The Trabe want
nothing more than that.

00:39:38.634 --> 00:39:42.866
The Trabe have always
wanted peace for themselves,

00:39:42.904 --> 00:39:45.168
but we paid the price.

00:39:45.207 --> 00:39:46.333
They lived in luxury

00:39:46.375 --> 00:39:48.400
and we lived
in squalor and misery.

00:39:48.443 --> 00:39:50.240
What I fear, Captain,

00:39:50.279 --> 00:39:52.645
is that this union
you've made with the Trabe

00:39:52.681 --> 00:39:55.650
is an effort to force us
to capitulate.

00:39:55.684 --> 00:39:59.882
If so, we assure you
it is doomed to failure.

00:39:59.921 --> 00:40:02.048
I won't pretend
that our alliance

00:40:02.090 --> 00:40:05.059
wasn't an attempt to
make a show of strength.

00:40:05.093 --> 00:40:07.960
Separately, we and the Trabe
are vulnerable.

00:40:07.996 --> 00:40:10.089
Together, we are stronger.

00:40:10.132 --> 00:40:13.260
Are you threatening us,
Captain?

00:40:13.302 --> 00:40:16.965
It is important that you
understand our determination,

00:40:17.072 --> 00:40:18.334
but it's not a threat.

00:40:18.373 --> 00:40:19.635
It's an offer.

00:40:19.675 --> 00:40:22.769
A negotiated peace
among all of us would provide

00:40:22.811 --> 00:40:24.676
a greater stability
in this Quadrant.

00:40:24.713 --> 00:40:27.477
How could that do anything
but benefit us all?

00:40:27.516 --> 00:40:30.974
I can't speak for all of you,

00:40:31.053 --> 00:40:35.251
but I, for one, don't think
we can trust this proposal.

00:40:35.290 --> 00:40:38.623
A woman and a Trabe...

00:40:38.660 --> 00:40:40.924
how can we listen to them?

00:40:40.962 --> 00:40:44.295
I find you nothing
but a hypocrite, Captain...

00:40:44.333 --> 00:40:47.268
allying yourself to the greatest
villains this Quadrant

00:40:47.302 --> 00:40:48.394
has ever known.

00:40:48.437 --> 00:40:49.995
If this is where your

00:40:50.038 --> 00:40:52.973
revered Federation values
have taken you,

00:40:53.008 --> 00:40:54.441
I want no part of it.

00:40:54.476 --> 00:40:58.640
Gentlemen, allow me to confer
with my Federation colleagues.

00:40:58.680 --> 00:41:01.240
Please, have some refreshments
and let us continue

00:41:01.283 --> 00:41:03.183
in a few moments.

00:41:03.218 --> 00:41:06.881
Captain, would you
please join me?

00:41:13.261 --> 00:41:17.220
Captain, I really need
to talk to you now.

00:41:18.900 --> 00:41:20.231
Get down!

00:41:22.371 --> 00:41:25.465
What is this, Captain?

00:41:25.507 --> 00:41:26.565
It's a trap!

00:41:26.608 --> 00:41:28.166
Take cover!

00:41:30.379 --> 00:41:32.210
Voyager, Red Alert.

00:41:32.247 --> 00:41:33.236
We're on it.

00:42:09.184 --> 00:42:11.277
You've ruined
what would have been

00:42:11.319 --> 00:42:13.947
the greatest step
toward peace in decades.

00:42:13.989 --> 00:42:16.048
Peace? A massacre?

00:42:16.091 --> 00:42:18.821
I could have decimated
the Kazon leadership.

00:42:18.860 --> 00:42:20.953
It would have taken them
years to recover.

00:42:20.996 --> 00:42:22.964
You planned this whole thing

00:42:22.998 --> 00:42:26.365
and used our goodwill to make
sure you were successful.

00:42:26.401 --> 00:42:27.766
You don't know the Kazon.

00:42:27.803 --> 00:42:29.703
There's no dealing with them.

00:42:29.738 --> 00:42:31.228
Violence is all they understand.

00:42:31.273 --> 00:42:33.468
Or perhaps it's all
you understand.

00:42:33.508 --> 00:42:35.237
You're naive, Captain.

00:42:35.277 --> 00:42:36.972
It's clear you have
no understanding

00:42:37.078 --> 00:42:39.308
of the harsh realities
of this part of space.

00:42:39.347 --> 00:42:41.315
What I tried to do was
done as much for you

00:42:41.349 --> 00:42:42.646
as it was for us.

00:42:42.684 --> 00:42:45.744
I'm not grateful,
and I want you off my ship.

00:42:45.787 --> 00:42:48.984
Chief, beam our former guest
back to his vessel.

00:42:49.024 --> 00:42:50.719
Captain, don't do this.

00:42:50.759 --> 00:42:51.726
You're going to need us.

00:42:51.760 --> 00:42:52.727
I don't think so.

00:42:52.761 --> 00:42:54.922
The Kazon will be determined
to seek revenge.

00:42:54.963 --> 00:42:57.329
How can this one ship
hope to survive?

00:42:57.365 --> 00:42:59.265
Not by making deals
with executioners.

00:42:59.301 --> 00:43:00.825
Energize.

00:43:06.041 --> 00:43:07.702
I would suggest we
depart before the Kazon

00:43:07.742 --> 00:43:09.300
have a chance to return
to their ships.

00:43:09.344 --> 00:43:11.335
Janeway to Paris.
Get us out of here.

00:43:11.379 --> 00:43:12.869
Aye, Captain.

00:43:21.490 --> 00:43:24.357
There's no question we're
more vulnerable now than ever.

00:43:24.392 --> 00:43:25.791
We have to take every measure

00:43:25.827 --> 00:43:27.954
to make sure we're prepared
for an attack.

00:43:28.063 --> 00:43:30.930
I want continual diagnostics
on all ship's systems.

00:43:30.966 --> 00:43:33.958
I will schedule additional
battle drills for all hands.

00:43:34.069 --> 00:43:36.094
Mr. Neelix,
what about our food supplies?

00:43:36.137 --> 00:43:37.627
We're in good shape, Captain.

00:43:37.672 --> 00:43:40.505
We shouldn't have to stop
anywhere for several weeks.

00:43:40.542 --> 00:43:42.510
Good. Lieutenant,
what's the condition

00:43:42.544 --> 00:43:44.307
of our propulsion systems?

00:43:44.346 --> 00:43:46.940
We have a reasonable
supply of antimatter.

00:43:46.982 --> 00:43:48.279
Barring any major problems,

00:43:48.316 --> 00:43:49.943
we should have
maximum performance

00:43:49.985 --> 00:43:52.146
of both warp
and impulse engines.

00:43:52.187 --> 00:43:54.849
There's just one more thing
I want to say.

00:43:54.890 --> 00:43:59.384
I hope there's a lesson
for all of us in this.

00:43:59.427 --> 00:44:00.416
Although some of the species

00:44:00.462 --> 00:44:01.986
we've encountered here
have been peaceful,

00:44:02.030 --> 00:44:05.693
others seem governed only
by their own self-interests.

00:44:05.734 --> 00:44:07.725
This appears to be
a region of space

00:44:07.769 --> 00:44:09.430
that doesn't have many rules.

00:44:09.471 --> 00:44:11.530
But I believe we can
learn something

00:44:11.573 --> 00:44:13.632
from the events
that have unfolded.

00:44:13.675 --> 00:44:16.269
In a part of space
where there are few rules,

00:44:16.311 --> 00:44:20.304
it's more important than ever
that we hold fast to our own.

00:44:20.348 --> 00:44:22.942
In a region where shifting
allegiances are commonplace,

00:44:23.018 --> 00:44:27.580
we have to have something
stable to rely on, and we do...

00:44:27.622 --> 00:44:30.955
the principles and ideals
of the Federation.

00:44:30.992 --> 00:44:33.620
As far as I'm concerned,

00:44:33.662 --> 00:44:38.232
those are the best allies
we could have.
